🌱 Garden Planner Directory Website Blueprint

1. 🎯 Core Purpose

A directory + planning hub where homeowners, DIY gardeners, landscapers, and small farms can:
•	Find local suppliers & services (nurseries, landscape companies, bulk mulch/topsoil, compost, tree removal, etc.).
•	Connect garden design planning tools (your Garden Planner) with real suppliers → e.g., a user designs a garden row with perennials, the site suggests nearby nurseries that carry them.
•	Build trust and visibility via reviews, certifications, and user-generated gardens.
 
2. 🗂 Site Structure

Main Categories (Top Menu)
1.	Garden Centers & Nurseries
2.	Landscaping Services
3.	Bulk Materials (mulch, soil, stone, compost)
4.	Tree & Shrub Services (tree removal, pruning, arborists)
5.	Greenhouses & Specialty Growers
6.	Native Plants & Sustainable Suppliers
7.	Garden Design Inspiration (connects directly to Garden Planner)

Subcategories (Filters & Directory Listings)
•	By Location: Buffalo, Rochester, Syracuse, Finger Lakes, Southern Tier, Lake Ontario Coast.
•	By Service Type: design, install, delivery, seasonal cleanup, irrigation, fencing, etc.
•	By Plant/Material Type: perennials, annuals, fruit trees, shrubs, compost, hardscape stone.
•	By Certifications: ecological, native plants, organic, licensed arborist, etc.
 
3. 💰 Monetization Model
1.	Freemium Listings
o	Basic listing: name, address, phone, website. Free.
o	Premium: photos, featured placement, logo, direct planner integration. $25–50/mo.
2.	Advertising Blocks
o	Contextual ads tied to categories (e.g., topsoil supplier ad shows up on “Soil” pages).
3.	Affiliate/Referral Links
o	Partner with seed/tool suppliers (Amazon, Johnny’s Seeds, Gardener’s Supply) → earn % from purchases.
4.	Planner Integration Add-Ons
o	Businesses can pay to have their products appear in your Garden Planner’s “Suggested Sources”.
5.	Seasonal Sponsorships
o	“Spring Planting Spotlight” for local garden centers.
o	“Fall Mulch Madness” promo for bulk suppliers.
 
4. ⚙️ Key Features
•	Search & Filter Directory: by ZIP code, category, plant type, service.
•	Map Integration: Google Maps pins for all listings.
•	Planner Tie-In: Users select a crop/row in the planner → sidebar shows suppliers nearby who carry it.
•	Reviews & Ratings: Verified buyers leave feedback.
•	Seasonal Content Hub: Articles/videos on planting in Zone 6, how-tos, etc.
•	User Showcase: Allow gardeners to upload photos of gardens designed with your planner, tagged with suppliers they used.
 
5. 📈 SEO & Keyword Anchors

Build landing pages around high-intent local searches (from our earlier keyword brainstorm):
•	“Garden Centers in Rochester NY”
•	“Bulk Mulch Delivery Buffalo NY”
•	“Native Plant Nurseries Western NY”
•	“Landscaping Services Syracuse NY”
•	“Tree Removal Rochester NY”
•	“Greenhouses in Western NY”

Each landing page = directory listings + integrated planner demo + content (guides, tips, photos).
 
6. 🚀 Launch Plan (90-Day Roadmap)

Phase 1 — MVP (Month 1–2)
•	Build basic directory framework (categories + filters).
•	Seed with 20–30 listings (pull from public info: top nurseries, landscapers, suppliers in WNY).
•	Integrate a lightweight version of Garden Planner (demo rows + call-to-action to try full planner).

Phase 2 — Growth (Month 3–4)
•	Add premium listing option (Stripe or PayPal).
•	Launch 3–5 SEO landing pages (optimized for local high-volume keywords).
•	Start email capture: “Download Free Planting Guide for WNY Gardeners.”

Phase 3 — Monetization (Month 5–6)
•	Approach local nurseries/landscapers → offer premium placement.
•	Add affiliate blocks for seeds/tools.
•	Roll out seasonal content hub.
 
